    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Revelations is the third studio album by Gene, released in 1999 on Polydor. It finds the band sharpening their Britpop-inflected rock into a harder, more direct sound, with an emphasis on punchy guitar work, dramatic melodies, and Martin Rossiter’s impassioned vocals. The album includes one of the group’s best-known singles, “As Good as It Gets,” and also features “Fill Her Up,” helping it reach the UK Top 30 and giving it a stronger commercial profile than much of the band’s later work.\n\nCritically, Revelations is often viewed as one of Gene’s most forceful and mature records, with a darker, more politically charged tone than their earlier albums. Songs such as “The British Disease” and “Mayday” reflect a band pushing beyond elegant indie craftsmanship toward a more urgent, arena-sized rock sound, while the closing tracks add a sense of scope and emotional weight. It stands as a late-Britpop album that combines strong songwriting with a more muscular production style, making it a notable entry in Gene’s catalogue.",
